{
  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only configuration (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool; config_005) achieves 0.650 acc, while adding resnet50 image with concat fusion (config_030) slightly *decreases* performance to 0.632. Image-only resnet50 is very weak (0.208). This raises the question of whether the slight multimodal drop is due to concat diluting the weak image signal or whether the image simply adds no useful information. Question: config_031 changes only the fusion from concat to weighted (keeping scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, multiprofile identical to config_030), isolating the fusion mechanism. If weighted fusion recovers or exceeds 0.650, it indicates the image carries signal that concat fails to leverage; if it remains near 0.632, it strongly suggests resnet50 features are not informative for this task and we should pivot to testing a stronger image encoder (ViT-L). Why best: It is a single-variable, controlled follow-up to the most recent multimodal result, directly resolving the key uncertainty about whether image fusion is the bottleneck before committing budget to larger architectural changes."
}

